# Bitirim Clothing Creator -- local configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the value. `.env` is git-ignored; this
# example file is not, and must never contain a real key.
#
# The key is read by the desktop host only, at the moment of an outbound
# request. It never reaches the interface, the generated JavaScript bundle,
# a log line, an error message or an exported project.

# Google AI Studio API key, from https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Used for AI texture generation (model: gemini-3.1-flash-image).
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Where the application looks, in order:
#   1. the GEMINI_API_KEY environment variable
#   2. a .env.local or .env file beside the application, or up to five folders above it
#   3. the key entered under Settings > AI, encrypted with Windows DPAPI
#
# An installed copy has no shell to export from, so (3) is the one most people
# will use. (1) and (2) are the development override.
